{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the children of Israel journeyed from Beeroth Bene-Jaakan, etc. — Now you may say to me: You say, ״And I prayed also for Aharon at that time״ — at the beginning of the forty [years], but we know that Aharon died, and if so, what did your prayer avail? Moshe said to them: He did not die at the beginning of the forty, in the episode of the calf, but at the end of the forty he died at Hor HaHar, at that time when they journeyed from Beeroth Bene-Jaakan, having come there from Moserot, as is written in the itinerary: ״ויסעו ממוסרות ויחנו בבני יעקן״ — ״and they journeyed from there to Hor HaHar״ — there Aharon died — and not in the episode of the calf." "And Elazar his son ministered in his stead — that he donned his father's garments there, and by a path of greatness and honor he died at the mouth of YHWH — this is its plain sense, for it is not written here ״ובני ישראל נסעו מבארת בני יעקן ויחנו במוסרה״ in the manner that I explained at ״מקברות התאוה נסעו העם חצרות״, where it does not write ״and they encamped at Hazeroth.״ So too here — ״ובני ישראל נסעו מבארות בני יעקן״ — which is at Moserah. Or go this way: from Beeroth Bene-Jaakan, when they came from Moserah. And our Rabbis derived from the variation of the verse what they derived."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:40.106425149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}